[] error|sites[10]|Duplicate host+port '*:8009' — already defined at sites[9]
[] error|sites[11].port|Port 8002 is already used by a TCP proxy site at sites[2]
[] error|sites[12].port|Port 8002 is already used by a TCP proxy site at sites[2]
[] error|sites[12].port|TCP proxy port 8002 conflicts with HTTP site '*:8002'
[] error|sites[14].tls.httpRedirectPort|HTTP port 8080 already redirects to HTTPS at sites[13].tls.httpRedirectPort
[] error|global.workers|must be greater than 0 (0 would run the server with no worker threads)
[redis,consumers] warning|rateLimit.store|multiple distinct Redis URLs configured across site/route/consumer rateLimit.store fields (redis://***@cache:6379, redis://route:6379, redis://cons:6379). Only one Redis connection is ever established per process — Conduit will connect to 'redis://***@cache:6379' and every other level configuring a different URL will silently share that same connection instead of getting its own. Point every level at the same Redis instance to avoid surprises.
[redis,!consumers] warning|rateLimit.store|multiple distinct Redis URLs configured across site/route/consumer rateLimit.store fields (redis://***@cache:6379, redis://route:6379). Only one Redis connection is ever established per process — Conduit will connect to 'redis://***@cache:6379' and every other level configuring a different URL will silently share that same connection instead of getting its own. Point every level at the same Redis instance to avoid surprises.
[forward-auth] error|sites[0].forwardAuth.url|forwardAuth.url points to 127.0.0.1:2019 — this is the Conduit Admin API. Routing external auth requests through the admin API is a security risk. Use a dedicated auth service instead.
[] error|sites[1].tls|Cannot combine 'acme' with 'cert'/'key' — use Auto-TLS or manual certificates, not both
